  "bodyTypst": "Consider the family of functions $f(x)= frac(1,x^(2)- 2 x + k)$, where $k$ is a constant.\n\n(a) Find the value of $k$, for $k > 0$, such that the slope of the line tangent to the graph of $f$ at $x = 0$ equals 6.\n\n(b) For $k = - 8$, find the value of $integral_(0)^(1) f(x) d x$.\n\n(c) For $k = 1$, find the value of $integral_(0)^(2) f(x) d x$ or show that it diverges.",
